From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Do not unwind past StackBase in the x64 handler search.

call_seh_handlers() checks the establisher frame of each unwound frame
against the stack limits and marks the exception EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID
when it falls outside, which corresponds to what Windows reports for a
frame outside the stack. That check runs only after the unwind, and
unwinding a leaf frame already reads the return address at Rsp. When an
earlier frame was misread, for example by the host unwinder, and left Rsp
less than one slot below StackBase or above it, that read went past the
thread stack. The resulting access violation was dispatched through the
same frames and failed the same way, so the process died in
RtlVirtualUnwind2() instead of reporting the original exception.

Before each unwind, check that the return address slot at Rsp lies below
StackBase, and otherwise end the search with EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID as
the establisher frame check would. A walk that ends exactly at StackBase
still stops as before, and the lower stack limit is left to the existing
establisher frame check, so behaviour only changes where the unwind would
have read past StackBase.

The change is not opt-in: it only replaces a fault inside ntdll with the
stack-invalid result the existing check already produces. RtlUnwindEx() is
left unchanged; it runs after a handler was found on a validated chain,
may already have called unwind handlers, and reports a bad stack
differently, so it needs a separate change.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c
index 8ac6c53..ce263e3 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -227,6 +227,19 @@ static DWORD call_seh_handler( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, ULONG_PTR frame,
 #endif
 
 
+/**********************************************************************
+ *           is_valid_unwind_rsp
+ *
+ * Unwinding a leaf frame reads the return address at Rsp before the
+ * establisher frame can be checked against the stack limits, so make sure
+ * that slot still lies below StackBase.
+ */
+static inline BOOL is_valid_unwind_rsp( ULONG64 rsp )
+{
+    return rsp <= (ULONG64)NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackBase - sizeof(ULONG64);
+}
+
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *           call_seh_handlers
  *
@@ -251,6 +264,14 @@ NTSTATUS call_seh_handlers( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, CONTEXT *orig_context )
     nested_frame = 0;
     for (;;)
     {
+        if (!is_valid_unwind_rsp( context.Rsp ))
+        {
+            ERR( "invalid stack pointer %p (%p-%p)\n", (void *)context.Rsp,
+                 NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackLimit, NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackBase );
+            rec->ExceptionFlags |= EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID;
+            break;
+        }
+
         status = virtual_unwind( UNW_FLAG_EHANDLER, &dispatch, &context );
         if (status != STATUS_SUCCESS) return status;
 
